# L §5.14 `move = "move" ID [binds] ...`, L §2.3 `bind = ID "in" (ID | ... | range)`, L §5.11 "A bind is over an
# index, a kind, a key list or a stepped range": a move keyed by a stepped range `n in 1 .. cnt` (integers, cnt a row).
# Three instances on first_day + n (2026-03-02, -03, -04), 100.00 PLN each: flows(pay, 2026) = 300.00 PLN (the move's
# amounts, L §5.14.3), konto 1 000 - 300 = 700.00 PLN; an instance is named by its keys like a def keyed by a range
# (`pay[k]`, L §2.5).
=== m.tally
model st
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input cnt: int
input first_day: date
input amt: money PLN

move pay[n in 1 .. cnt]: transfers
  on add_days(first_day, n)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cnt = 3
  first_day = 2026-03-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q1: flows(pay, 2026), bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
ask q2: pay[k].day for k in 1 .. cnt
ask q3: flows(pay[k], 2026) for k in 2 .. 2
=== expect
q1: (300.00 PLN, 700.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2 (k = 1): 2026-03-02
  cut 2026-01-01
q2 (k = 2): 2026-03-03
  cut 2026-01-01
q2 (k = 3): 2026-03-04
  cut 2026-01-01
q3 (k = 2): 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
